{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"9b77fca3437450ae","type":"text","text":"## **Original novel | Chapter V: Advice from a Caterpillar**\n*Lewis Carroll, Alice’s Adventures in Wonderland (1865)*\n\n> The Caterpillar and Alice looked at each other for some time in silence: at last the Caterpillar took the hookah out of its mouth, and addressed her in a languid, sleepy voice.\n\n> ‘Who are you?’ said the Caterpillar.\n\n> This was not an encouraging opening for a conversation. Alice replied, rather shyly, ‘I--I hardly know, sir, just at present-- at least I know who I was when I got up this morning, but I think I must have been changed several times since then.’\n\n> ‘What do you mean by that?’ said the Caterpillar sternly. ‘Explain yourself!’\n\n> ‘I can't explain myself, I'm afraid, sir’ said Alice, ‘because I'm not myself, you see.’\n\n> ‘I don't see,’ said the Caterpillar.\n\n> ‘I'm afraid I can't put it more clearly,’ Alice replied very politely, ‘for I can't understand it myself to begin with; and being so many different sizes in a day is very confusing.’","x":1140,"y":-335,"width":830,"height":705},
		{"id":"402bcb23fd2a4e4e","type":"text","text":"## **Context and vocabulary support**\nAlice has changed size several times and meets a Caterpillar who asks a difficult question.\n\n**Mini-glossary outside the original:**\n*Caterpillar* = rups\n*languid* = loom\n*sternly* = streng\n\n","x":1140,"y":400,"width":830,"height":235,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"0e33ba0e43cf7d50","type":"text","text":"# **Today's class**\n### Alice in Wonderland | Lesson 2 of 3\n","x":-812,"y":-558,"width":650,"height":140,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"138f1cb64f85567b","type":"text","text":"### **08:15** Introduction: The Caterpillar\n### **08:20** Read and skim\n### **08:30** Word meaning + false friends\n### **08:35** Grammar + advice\n### **08:45** Exit ticket","x":-812,"y":-388,"width":650,"height":270,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"f3fa5a630ebd8478","type":"text","text":"# **Homework | 27 November**\n- Write an **8-line dialogue** between Alice and a friend. Use at least **one present perfect form** and **two modals**.\n- Upload at least **two unfamiliar words** from the passage, or words you would like to use more, to Google Classroom.\n- Finish any unfinished assigned workbook tasks. Upload your completed Lesson 2 workbook in Google Classroom and click **Turn in**.","x":-812,"y":-88,"width":650,"height":340,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"44a5f97dd3995de7","type":"text","text":"## **Big question**\nWho are you? Why does Alice struggle to answer?","x":158,"y":-360,"width":600,"height":112,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"a5436460730e2406","type":"text","text":"## **Learning goals**\n**I can:**\n- Explain Alice’s problem in one sentence.\n- Copy one relevant clue word-for-word.\n- Infer tone and word meaning from context.\n- Recognise and explain false friends.\n- Use the present perfect to describe experiences.\n- Give supportive advice and express absence of obligation.","x":158,"y":-219,"width":600,"height":315,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"41c61f19364c69e2","type":"text","text":"## **Retrieval and prediction | Q1**\n**Retrieval:** What happened to Alice in Lesson 1? Give one example with *should*.\n\n**Prediction:** Read the context note. Write **one possible reason** someone might feel confused about who they are.","x":158,"y":120,"width":600,"height":235,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"ea9eb53acdd14b09","type":"text","text":"## **Instruction 1 | False friends**\nFalse friends look or sound similar in two languages but have different meanings.\n\n| English            | Dutch meaning         | False Friend |\n| ------------------ | --------------------- | ------------ |\n| Eventually         | Uiteindelijk          | Eventueel    |\n| Actual             | Werkelijk / feitelijk |              |\n| Actually           | Eigenlijk / in feite  |              |\n| Possibly / perhaps | Eventueel / misschien |              |\n| Current / topical  | Actueel               |              |\n\nUse the context rather than translating a word just because it looks familiar.","x":2088,"y":-407,"width":700,"height":425,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"409e1ed3a40340cb","type":"text","text":"## **Instruction 2 | Present perfect**\n**Subject + have/has + past participle**\n- Alice has changed.\n- Alice has not changed.\n- Has Alice changed?\n\nUse the present perfect for experiences without a specified finished time, or past events connected to the present.\n\n**Compare:** *Alice changed yesterday* (finished time) and *Alice has changed several times today* (ongoing time period).\n\nCarroll uses the more complex form *must have been changed*. We practise Grammar 3 separately.\n\n**B2 extension:** Complete the additional tense items in Q7, justify present perfect vs. past simple, and write an affirmative sentence, a negative sentence and a question.","x":2088,"y":43,"width":700,"height":490,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"cf068e44342646c0","type":"text","text":"## **Instruction 3 | Advice and obligation**\n| Structure | Function |\n| --- | --- |\n| Should / shouldn't | Advice / negative advice |\n| Could | Suggestion |\n| Mustn't | Prohibition |\n| Doesn't have to | Absence of obligation |\n\nUse the base form after a modal or *doesn't have to*.\n\n**Compare:**\n- Alice shouldn't answer the question.\n- Alice doesn't have to answer the question.\n- Alice mustn't answer the question.\n\nWhich expresses advice, absence of obligation or prohibition? Explain your choices.\n\n","x":2088,"y":563,"width":700,"height":491,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"9407198184c74df2","type":"text","text":"## **Vocabulary support | Q8**\n| English | Dutch |\n| --- | --- |\n| To express | Uitdrukken / aangeven |\n| Advice | Advies / raad |\n| Absence | Afwezigheid / het ontbreken van |\n| Obligation | Verplichting |\n| Absence of obligation | Geen verplichting |\n| Prohibition | Verbod |\n| To be required to | Verplicht zijn om |\n| To be allowed to | Mogen |\n| Necessary | Noodzakelijk |\n| Permission | Toestemming |\n\n**Sentence starter:** This sentence expresses ... because ...","x":2866,"y":844,"width":660,"height":420,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"0bdc494487051592","type":"text","text":"## **Exit ticket | Q9**\nName Alice’s feeling in **ONE word** and give **ONE exact clue** from the text.\n\n","x":2088,"y":1144,"width":630,"height":120,"color":"1"}
	],
